# Enhanced Mail Merge to Email (Word VBA)

A Microsoft Word macro that sends a mail merge as individual Outlook emails. Word's built-in "Send Email Messages" can't do most of what this macro adds:

- **CC and BCC**, and several To / CC / BCC addresses per recipient
- **A different subject per recipient**
- **Attachments**, one or more per recipient
- **Importance, sensitivity, read receipts and delivery receipts**
- **Delayed delivery**, so emails are sent at a set date or time
- **Send on behalf of** another address
- **Send now, or save as drafts** to check first
- **Problem rows are saved as drafts** listing what's wrong, instead of being skipped without warning
- **A progress log** that records every email, so you can **resume** after an error or after stopping early
- **Batch runs**, to process e.g. 20 emails at a time
- **Stop safely** at any time with the Esc key

Each email is set up from columns in your mail merge data source, such as an Excel sheet or CSV file.

